# US-125266 — EPQ: Triggers to Reload Tax Lines for DLQ Check After Agency Calendar Date Changes — Detailed Analysis

> Module: Business Tools → Exception Processing Queue (EPQ) → Delinquent Installment Search (DIR).
> Database: `LASTax` (plus read-only cross-database reads from `LASTotalTaxSolution` and `LASCommon`).
> No application code (DAL/BLL/UI/Dispatcher) is affected — this is a SQL-only change to a
> SQL-Agent-scheduled batch process with no C# caller anywhere in the codebase.

---

## 1. Overview

This story fixes two independent reliability/correctness gaps in the nightly EPQ batch process that
creates and maintains Delinquent Installment Search (DIR) work items:

- **Gap 1 (reliability):** The batch (`usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew`, run by SQL Agent job
  `LAS_ExceptionProcessQueue_DataImportNew`) decides DIR eligibility using an exact
  `DATEDIFF(DAY, ELD date, GETDATE()) = 20` match against a single ELD date, with no mechanism to react
  to later changes in that ELD date or to catch up on a missed match day. Compounding this, a recently
  deployed duplicate-prevention guard (`usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU`, from US-120627) fully
  suppresses *all* further processing — including legitimate date refreshes — once a DIR item exists and
  is open for a given loan/agency/tax combination. Net effect: once an ELD date changes after a DIR item
  already exists (open or not), nothing about that item is ever updated again by this batch.
- **Gap 2 (correctness):** No validation anywhere in the eligibility path confirms an installment
  belongs to the current tax year before a new DIR record is created/loaded. A correction to a prior
  (historical, already-closed) tax year's calendar data can therefore incorrectly satisfy the 20-day rule
  and generate a brand-new DIR work item for data that is not an active, current issue.

Both gaps live entirely inside two existing stored procedures in `LASTax`. No new tables, no DAL/BLL/UI
changes, and no dispatcher changes are required.

