## 3. Database Changes

**Database:** `LASTax`. No schema changes — both affected objects are stored procedures only. No new
tables or columns; all fields referenced already exist.

### 3.1 ELD date selection (tie-break correction)

Per PO direction ("use story #129258 to get ELD rules"), the oldest non-null date among `ELD0`/`ELDH`/
`ELDX` must win (tie-break: `ELDH` > `ELDX` > `ELD0`), not the latest as currently deployed:

```sql
-- Current (incorrect per PO direction):
ORDER BY v.DueDate DESC, CASE v.RunCode WHEN 'ELDH' THEN 1 WHEN 'ELDX' THEN 2 ELSE 3 END

-- Required:
ORDER BY v.DueDate ASC, CASE v.RunCode WHEN 'ELDH' THEN 1 WHEN 'ELDX' THEN 2 ELSE 3 END
```

This also brings the live SP in line with the existing (never-deployed) tSQLt test
`[test_usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNew].[test_ELD_Logic_US129258]`, which already expects this ordering.

### 3.2 Eligibility window (reliability fix)

Current logic requires an exact match:

```sql
WHERE DATEDIFF(DAY, w.DueDate, @Getdate) = @StartDays
```

This must become reactive to ELD date changes rather than a single-day snapshot, and must correctly
distinguish "update an existing item" from "create a new item" (see §3.3) rather than relying solely on
the US-120627 guard to prevent duplicates. Exact WHERE-clause mechanics (e.g., whether to use `>=
@StartDays`, and whether to retain `@EndDays` — currently fetched but unused — as an upper bound) are an
implementation-time decision, not fixed by this document.

### 3.3 Dedup guard carve-out (`usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU`)

The existing US-120627 guard:

```sql
IF @WinnerExceptionID IS NOT NULL
BEGIN
    -- log to DedupLog, mark staging processed, RETURN — suppresses everything
END
```

must be extended so that when the incoming ELD-derived value differs from what is already stored for
that record, the procedure proceeds to **update** the existing record (ELD date, SLA/reporting due date,
Load/Date-Added — see §14) rather than suppressing it. When nothing has actually changed, the existing
suppression behavior is preserved (per PO Answer #3: "system updates the record and does not create a
duplicate record").

### 3.4 Tax-year validation (new)

The existing cursor body declares `@CurrentTaxYear`/`@InstallmentNo` but never assigns or uses them in
the DIR eligibility branch:

```sql
IF (@DLQResearchFlag = '1') ... -- no tax-year check present anywhere in this branch today
```

A new validation must be added before the DIR eligibility flag is set, so that prior-tax-year
installments cannot satisfy the rule. The exact comparison source for "current tax year" (per agency,
not a single system-wide year — see §14) still requires final confirmation before implementation.

