## 13. Edge Cases

| Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Two of ELD0/ELDH/ELDX share the exact same (oldest) date | Tie-break: `ELDH` > `ELDX` > `ELD0` |
| An installment has no ELD0/ELDH/ELDX on file at all | Excluded from DIR eligibility — unchanged existing behavior |
| A single loan has multiple parcels/TaxIDs under one agency | Each TaxID evaluated independently — confirmed via live discovery data (e.g., Loan 15016876 / Agency 370020000 spans 6+ distinct TaxIDs) |
| A DIR item is already Completed | ELD date, SLA/reporting due date, and Load/Date-Added fields are refreshed; `isComplete`/`isFollowUp` are left untouched; the item is never reopened (PO Answer #3, #5; AC #4–#5) |
| DMU/TSP SystemCodes pass through the same shared `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` | Must remain provably unaffected — all new logic explicitly scoped to `SystemCode = 'DIR'` (see §13 comparative analysis below) |
| A correction to a prior-tax-year record satisfies the 20-day rule | Excluded from new-record creation by the new tax-year validation (§3.4) |
| Installments already missing a DIR record as of today (e.g., the Allegheny example) | **Not** retroactively created by this fix — this is a go-forward-only change (PO Answer #2, #6). A live discovery query identified 637 such gaps system-wide as of 2026-10-30 (76 under tax year 2026, 548 under 2025, 13 under 2024) — provided to PO/Ops for review, not remediated by this story |

### DMU/TSP comparative analysis summary (PO Answer #7)

| Queue | Eligibility driver | Uses ELD0/ELDH/ELDX? |
|---|---|---|
| DIR | The 20-day ELD-calendar rule (`#tbl_DLQ_Installment_Research`) | Yes — the only one |
| DMU | `DelqInd`/`DateDownInd` lien-level flags, unrelated to the calendar | No |
| TSP | Presence in `lat_RPT_TDR360`/`lat_RPT_TDD360`/`tbl_cta_ReportedItems` | No for eligibility; yes for a secondary display-only due date, via the separate function `lat_GET_ELDDate` |

**Conclusion:** Gap 1 (the ELD-reliability bug) has no direct equivalent in DMU or TSP, since neither
uses the same eligibility mechanism — no change to their eligibility logic is required. The real shared
risk is that `usp_ExceptionQueue_DataImportNewIU` is called identically for all three `SystemCode`
values; every new carve-out in §3.3 must be explicitly conditioned on `SystemCode = 'DIR'`.

**Flag for PO confirmation:** `lat_GET_ELDDate` (used only by TSP) was itself modified 8 days before this
story's DIR-side change (US-134881, same author) to use the **greatest** date — the opposite rule from
what this story now applies to DIR. Recommend confirming with PO/Tharangini that this divergence between
DIR (oldest) and TSP (greatest) is intentional before finalizing.

