## 14. Assumptions

- "Use story #129258 to get ELD rules" (PO Answer #1) is interpreted as: oldest non-null value among
  ELD0/ELDH/ELDX wins, tie-break `ELDH` > `ELDX` > `ELD0` — matching the existing (never-deployed) tSQLt
  test for US-129258.
- "Load Dates" (PO Answer #4) is interpreted as `tbl_ExceptionQueue.InsertedDate`, displayed as
  "Date Added" on the live DIR screen. Per the PO's earlier worked example, this field is expected to be
  recalculated for Open/New items when the underlying ELD date changes — not treated as an immutable
  creation timestamp in this case.
- The exact source/formula for "current tax year" (§3.4) is **not yet finalized** — PO confirmed the
  *scope* (forward-only, no retroactive changes to existing EPQ records) but not the precise comparison
  value. An initial attempt to proxy this as "the latest tax year on file per agency" was tested against
  live Allegheny data and proven incorrect (it excluded the genuinely-overdue 2026 record in favor of an
  already-loaded, not-yet-due 2027 record). This must be resolved before §3.4 can be implemented.
- No DMU/TSP eligibility-logic changes are in scope for this story (see §13 comparative analysis);
  mitigation is explicit `SystemCode = 'DIR'` scoping of all new logic in the shared procedure.
- The 637-record discovery findings are for PO/Ops visibility only; no one-time data-correction script
  (e.g., for the Allegheny example) is in scope for this story, per PO Answer #2 ("we cannot update
  existing or older records in EPQ") combined with PO Answer #6 (requesting a list, not a fix). This
  reading has not yet received a single explicit PO confirmation and should be verified.
- Whether Tax Year 2025 (548 of the 637 discovered gaps) counts as "current" or "historical" for the
  affected agencies has not been confirmed by PO/Ops — treated as closed/historical for planning purposes
  per the user's working instruction ("for now"), leaving 76 records (Tax Year 2026) as the actionable
  current-year count. This is provisional and should be revisited once PO/Ops confirm.

